FILED s531b (Opus, 2026-11-01), found re-causing Mojo-DOM58 collection.t's *PLAN* row, whose key #564 is DONE (#564 fixed the SILENT half: the statement is now refused loudly; the feature itself has no task).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s531b/p-localglob.pl):
  no strict 'refs';
  my $caller = "main";
  our ($x, $y) = ("x0", "y0");
  { local (*{"${caller}::x"}, *{"${caller}::y"}) = (\"x1", \"y1"); print "$x $y\n" }
  print "$x $y\n";
perl 5.40.3: x1 y1 / x0 y0
PCL (main ade297e7): `PCL: statement dropped at ... line 4: local (*{"${caller}::x"}, ...) -- Parser2 TODO: unsupported `local` target: *{"${caller}::x"}`, then the run dies at the statement.

In the board: Mojo-DOM58 t/collection.t runs 15 rows and stops (rc 255, no plan) at lib/Mojo/DOM58/_Collection.pm:101 `local (*{"${caller}::a"}, *{"${caller}::b"}) = (\$a, \$b);` (the List::Util-style $a/$b aliasing of a sort/reduce callback).  Siblings: #540, #652 (other `local` target shapes), #3470 (a deref inside a parenthesised local LIST, completed).

=== DONE (s533c) ===
(Opus 5.5, 2026-11-04.)  A glob target in a `local` LIST is a `glob` item of the structured `local` lowering (Parser2::_local_glob_item): localized by the glob family's own open -- p-local-glob for `*NAME` / `*Pkg::NAME`, p-local-glob-dynamic for `*{EXPR}` / `*$x` / a punctuation glob -- whose value is the right side's element at the glob's static position, `(p-aref-deref RHS-TMP i)`; the right side is computed once, first; under an if/unless modifier the opens take the condition temporary.  A glob after an array / hash / slice target refuses (the position is not static; rule 12 -> the statement's announced drop).  The plain list assignment `(*x, *y) = LIST` is a separate silent no-op, FILED #4442 (the local list does not go through it).
Probes (scratch/s533c/p/g3.pl, g4.pl) == perl 5.40.3: the reproducer, the Mojo::DOM58 sort-callback idiom per iteration, a scalar + a glob, `= \*Other`, nested same name, one-element list, the other slots kept and restored, a bare list clears, if 0 / if 1, through a die, a called sub sees it.  Guard Pl/t/local-stmt-01.t rows 1-6 (fail on 0f2db817).
Board: Mojo-DOM58 t/collection.t one-file run 19 / 1 (was 14 / 1, rc 255, no plan); the `*PLAN*` row left baselines/cpan-board14-fails.tsv BY EDIT; row 6 `first` stays (#3550).
The same item fixes a SILENT WRONG the wide emission A/B found (s534): a LITERAL glob list `local (*FH, *A)` compiled on 0f2db817 to `(let ((*FH (make-p-box nil)) (*A (make-p-box nil))) …)` -- Lisp variables named *FH, never the glob -- so nothing was localized (probe scratch/s533c/p/lg.pl: inside, perl and the tree see FH closed and $A undef, the base sees both untouched).  Core sites: IPC/Cmd.pm (six handles), File/Compare.pm (*FROM, *TO), ExtUtils/Install.pm (*CMD, *SRC).


